    "notes": "issuers of 32 bytes 0x80 and 32 bytes 0x7f: bytes compare unsigned, so 0x7f is lower. a language with signed bytes that compares them as numbers gets it backwards. expected order computed with core's rule (asset type, code bytes with zero padding, issuer key bytes; isPoolShareAssetValid in stellar-core v30.0.0 src/util/types.cpp and the xdrpp union and xarray comparisons it uses), checked against stellar-xdr's derived Ord. pool_id cases expect the id core derives (sha256 of LiquidityPoolParameters with fee 30) when a < b, and a refusal otherwise, because core answers CHANGE_TRUST_MALFORMED for parameters that are not strictly ordered.",
